# === External public sibling repos (Apr 2026, moved under xenia/ Jun 2026) ===
# xenia-wire and xenia-peer are public standalone repos, nested under
# xenia/ as siblings of the monorepo's existing subprojects for
# convenience. They have their own git history — DO NOT commit
# them into the monorepo.
# (xenia-server was renamed to xenia-peer per the M0 release; keep
# both ignores so neither state resurfaces as untracked noise. The
# repos used to live at monorepo root — hence the old /xenia-wire/,
# /xenia-server/, /xenia-peer/ rules — but moved under xenia/ and the
# rules were never updated, which is why `git status` showed the
# whole xenia/ tree as untracked until this fix.)
/xenia/xenia-wire/
/xenia/xenia-server/
/xenia/xenia-peer/

# Externally-prepared Xenia patch trains land at repo root as scratch
# files, get applied into xenia/xenia-wire or xenia/xenia-peer, then
# should be deleted — not left as clutter (2026-07 cleanup removed
# ~23GB of archived build-artifact snapshots plus 20 stale/applied
# root-level .patch files; see xenia/XENIA_COMPREHENSIVE_REVIEW_2026-07.md).
/xenia-*.patch
/_patchwork/
.aider*

# === Monorepo Scratch & Tool Cleanup ===
fix_*.py
repair_*.py
patch_*.py

# Discarded environment backups
**/_archive-*/
**/_archive-disabled-*/
**/_archive-infrastructure-*/
